---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Data Inspector">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: September 8, 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Information we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Data Inspector may collect account details such as your name, email address, profile image, and authentication provider information when you sign in. Website requirements and uploaded images are stored when you submit them.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">How we use information</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We use this information to authenticate users, maintain accounts, display submitted requirements, support ownership controls, and operate the application. We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Third-party login</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">You may sign in using Google or Facebook. Those providers process information according to their own privacy policies. We receive only the information permitted by the provider and configured for this application.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Data retention and security</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We retain account and submitted content while it is needed to provide the service. We use reasonable safeguards to protect stored information, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">For privacy questions or data requests, contact the application owner through the contact details associated with this application.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
